The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
mdelay(MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS);
reg = mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT);
if ((reg & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) != CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF)
```
Reason:
The code assumes that the MCP251x device will enter configuration mode within a fixed delay of 5ms after a reset. If the device takes longer to stabilize, the read operation may return an incorrect state, leading to a failure in detecting the device's readiness and returning an error prematurely.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
timeout = jiffies + HZ;
while ((mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT) & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) !=
       CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF) {
    usleep_range(MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000,
                 MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000 * 2);
    if (time_after(jiffies, timeout)) {
        dev_err(&spi->dev,
            "MCP251x didn't enter in conf mode after reset\n");
        return -EBUSY;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a loop that continuously checks the device's state until it enters configuration mode or a timeout occurs. This allows for more time for the device to stabilize, accommodating boards that require longer than 5ms to power up, thus preventing premature errors.

